# Local dev secrets for the blog worker (gitignored as `.dev.vars`).
# `lunora dev` / the Vite dev server offer to generate `.dev.vars` from this
# file on first run — secret placeholders below are auto-filled. Or by hand:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars   # then fill in
#
# Generate a strong secret with: openssl rand -hex 32

# Required — the worker throws "AUTH_SECRET is required" without it.
AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32"

# Optional, LOCAL ONLY — the Vite dev origin (`server.port` in vite.config.ts).
# `@lunora/auth` treats an `http://localhost` value as port-agnostic: it derives
# the origin from each request, so auth keeps working if Vite falls back to
# another port, and this value is only the fallback. Keeping an explicit
# `http://` origin here is what marks the worker as local dev (no `Secure` flag
# on session cookies). Never put it in `wrangler.jsonc` `vars`, which ship with
# the deployed worker; left unset there, better-auth resolves the HTTPS origin
# per request.
AUTH_URL="http://localhost:5175"

# Required as soon as you use the featured-image upload: `@lunora/storage` signs
# the direct-to-R2 PUT URL with it, and `getSignedUrl`/`generateUploadUrl` throw
# without it. Any long random string — generate one the same way as AUTH_SECRET.
# There is no storage base URL to set: the upload URL is signed against the
# origin the request reached the worker on, which also serves the PUT.
STORAGE_SECRET="replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32"

# The origin the SchedulerDO dispatches `ctx.scheduler` jobs back into — this
# dev server. The DO reads it off its own env only (a caller-supplied target
# would be an SSRF vector), so it cannot follow the request the way the upload
# URL does. wrangler.jsonc ships it empty; set the deployed worker's public URL
# there before deploying.
LUNORA_ORIGIN_URL="http://localhost:5175"
